# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, used by scripts/container/sanitizer-steps.sh.
# Keep each entry narrow and explained; never suppress a report in the binding's own code.

# RR core discovery: lock-order inversion between Discovery_findservicebytype::work_lock (M0)
# and the work_lock (M1) of the Discovery_updatediscoverednodes object that
# Discovery::AsyncUpdateDetectedNodes creates fresh for each call. The calling thread takes M1
# exactly once, at the top of UpdateDiscoveredNodes, while holding M0. The callbacks that take
# M1 then M0 (getdetectednodes_callback / timeout_timer_callback -> InvokeHandler -> find2) are
# bound inside that critical section, so none can hold M1 before it, and the caller never asks
# for M1 again: the cycle cannot close. Reviewed against RR core; see PROGRESS.md, 2026-11-26.
deadlock:Discovery_updatediscoverednodes::UpdateDiscoveredNodes
